NS-3 Smart Grid Simulation

This folder contains representative smart grid communication simulation configurations used to generate communication traffic samples for latency analysis.

The simulation environment models HAN–NAN–WAN smart grid communication architecture under periodic and burst traffic conditions.

Representative parameters include:

- Packet size: 64–512 bytes
- Communication delay: 1–5 ms
- Traffic type: periodic and event-driven
- Queue model: DropTail
- Routing approach: adaptive communication routing

The generated traffic traces were used for transformer-based latency prediction experiments.
